abla F(E)} \mathrm{d}\operatorname{vol}. \end{equation} The measurability and countable additivity in this definition are standard properties of the subgradient map; see for example [ Section 2.1 , Fig17 ] . Proposition A.4.2 . Suppose that $F\in C^{1,1}(N_{\mathbb {R}})\cap \mathrm{Conv}(N_{\mathbb {R}})$. Fix an identification $N=\mathbb {Z}^ n$. Then \[  \operatorname{MA}_{\mathbb {R}}F=n!\cdot \det 
