3$ and use coordinates that are unitary at the point. Direct antisymmetrization gives \[  \bar\partial \gamma =-\frac{\mathrm i}{2}\sum _{a,b,c} \overline{T_{bc\bar a}}\, \mathrm{d}z^ a\wedge \mathrm{d}\bar z^ b\wedge \mathrm{d}\bar z^ c.  \] We use $\bar\partial \gamma ^{n-2}=(n-2)\bar\partial \gamma \wedge \gamma ^{n-3}$. To write the contraction explicitly, put \[  \delta ^{paj}_{bci} =\det \begin{pmatrix}  \delta _{pb}

